1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:03,354
This sentence came
in a CSS exam.

2
00:00:03,394 --> 00:00:04,920
Can you find
the error?

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:11,070
Most students attack
the verb ‘is’.

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:12,853
But the verb
is fine.

5
00:00:12,893 --> 00:00:15,476
The real problem
is the word ‘each’.

6
00:00:16,103 --> 00:00:17,694
‘Each’ means
we pick things

7
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:18,717
one by one:

8
00:00:18,757 --> 00:00:20,584
each chair,
each table,

9
00:00:20,624 --> 00:00:21,691
each sofa.

10
00:00:21,731 --> 00:00:22,897
So ‘each’ needs
something you

11
00:00:22,937 --> 00:00:24,109
can count.

12
00:00:24,737 --> 00:00:27,071
But furniture
is not one object.

13
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:28,140
It’s a unit:

14
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,871
chairs,
tables and sofas

15
00:00:29,911 --> 00:00:32,524
grouped together
and named as one.

16
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:33,432
A unit means one,

17
00:00:33,472 --> 00:00:34,695
and you can’t
pick ‘each’ out

18
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:35,815
of one.

19
00:00:36,537 --> 00:00:37,981
So we give
‘each’ something

20
00:00:38,021 --> 00:00:39,263
countable to hold:

21
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:40,171
a piece.

22
00:00:40,211 --> 00:00:42,023
Each piece
of furniture.

23
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:43,996
‘Each piece
of furniture

24
00:00:44,036 --> 00:00:45,808
in this display
is on sale for

25
00:00:45,848 --> 00:00:47,460
half price.’

26
00:00:48,403 --> 00:00:50,064
Logic, not rules.

27
00:00:50,104 --> 00:00:52,257
Comment ‘logic’
for the next one.

